The overall goal for this bug is to allow a xform author the same capability in our xf:input that they already have with an html:input w.r.t. fixing the size of the input field.  Web form authors often like to set how many characters wide a input field is and to set the maximum number of characters that can be input into the field.  html:input can achieve this with @size and @maxlength.

The end result of an offline discussion that Allan, Olli, Doron and I have had so far is that allowing @maxlength and @size as acceptable attributes on a xf:input is not desirable.  Instead of @size, the form author should use CSS to set the width of the field.

@maxlength is a tougher issue to tackle.  The overwhelming opinion is that we should tie the control tighter to the schema type and base the rendering of the control off of the limitations placed on the schema type.  For example, based on the maximum allowable value of a decimal-based type, only have the control accept enough characters to reach that limit and no more.

