When I click the archive button(s) I'd like to be able to ask for some user input, do some file handling etc. prior to the actual displacement of the message to it's archive folder.
Ideal would be to be able to override the archive function. As an example, the SendMessage function from "MsgComposeCommands.js" can be overridden like this.
If the overriding function returns true the archiving may continue, if the overriding function returns false, the archive call would be canceled.

Something like:
var ArchiveFunOriginal = Archive;
var Archive = function() {
  if (!CheckUserConfirmation())
    return;
  else{
    ArchiveFunOriginal.apply(this, arguments)
  }
};

